{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to share a backend engineering finding. While testing an unrelated bulk-import client yesterday, I measured legitimate synchronization bursts of 145 requests in a minute. Our load replay confirms the policy needs an ordinary API-key limit of exactly 150 requests per minute with a 60-second burst window. I hadn't updated the draft because the client test was owned by another team, but this is release-impacting — the current 100 requests per minute limit would throttle legitimate customer traffic."}
```

